('115.17.b.20',4,'In a healthy friendship, each person...','["respects the other''s boundaries", "pressures the other", "controls the other", "keeps secrets that hurt"]'::jsonb,0,'Boundaries matter.','original'),
('115.17.b.20',4,'A sign of an unhealthy relationship is...','["helping", "one person controlling or threatening the other", "sharing laughter", "taking turns"]'::jsonb,1,'Control is a warning sign.','original'),
('115.17.b.21.A',4,'Sexual harassment includes...','["class discussions", "group projects", "unwanted sexual comments or behavior", "friendly waves"]'::jsonb,2,'Harassment is unwelcome behavior.','original'),
('115.17.b.21.A',4,'Sexual abuse is...','["a friendly hug", "a game", "a handshake", "any sexual contact or behavior that is forced or not allowed by law"]'::jsonb,3,'It is never the child''s fault.','original'),
('115.17.b.21.A',4,'Sex trafficking is...','["forcing a person into sexual acts for money", "a sport", "a vacation", "a job fair"]'::jsonb,0,'It is a crime.','original'),
('115.17.b.21.B',4,'If someone is touching you in a way that makes you uncomfortable, you should tell...','["nobody", "a trusted adult such as a parent, teacher, or counselor", "a stranger", "an online friend"]'::jsonb,1,'Trusted adults can protect you.','original'),
('115.17.b.21.B',4,'You can report suspected abuse by telling a trusted adult or calling...','["a store", "a restaurant", "a child abuse hotline", "a bus driver"]'::jsonb,2,'Hotlines provide help.','original'),
('115.17.b.21.C',4,'A refusal skill when someone gives unwanted touch is to...','["laugh", "stay silent", "give in", "say \"No!\" loudly and go to a trusted adult"]'::jsonb,3,'You have the right to say no.','original'),
('115.17.b.21.C',4,'Your body belongs to...','["you", "whoever asks", "everyone", "nobody"]'::jsonb,0,'You decide who touches you.','original'),
('115.17.b.21.D',4,'Setting personal boundaries means deciding...','["to ignore your comfort", "what you are comfortable with and saying so", "to hide your feelings", "to let everyone decide for you"]'::jsonb,1,'Boundaries protect you.','original'),
('115.17.b.21.D',4,'Making decisions about personal boundaries is important to protect your...','["hair color", "lunch", "safety and well-being", "shoe size"]'::jsonb,2,'Boundaries keep you safe.','original'),
('115.17.b.22.A',4,'Puberty can bring physical changes such as...','["losing teeth", "shrinking", "a new skeleton", "growth spurts and body hair"]'::jsonb,3,'Puberty changes bodies.','original'),
('115.17.b.22.A',4,'During puberty, social and emotional changes can include...','["stronger moods and new interests", "no friendships", "no feelings", "only sleeping"]'::jsonb,0,'Emotions can shift.','original'),
('115.17.b.22.A',4,'A changing voice is one change that occurs during puberty for...','["nobody", "males", "only teachers", "only babies"]'::jsonb,1,'Voice deepens in many males.','original'),
('115.17.b.22.B',4,'The menstrual cycle usually repeats about every...','["2 days", "2 years", "28 days", "100 days"]'::jsonb,2,'The average cycle is about 28 days.','original'),
('115.17.b.22.B',4,'During the menstrual cycle, an egg is released from an...','["lung", "stomach", "kidney", "ovary"]'::jsonb,3,'Ovulation occurs in the ovary.','original'),
('115.17.b.22.C',4,'Hormones are chemical messengers that help the body...','["grow and develop", "stop moving", "forget", "shrink"]'::jsonb,0,'Hormones guide development.','original'),
('115.17.b.22.C',4,'Secondary sex characteristics are changes such as...','["fingerprints", "body hair and breast development", "blood type", "eye color"]'::jsonb,1,'These appear during puberty.','original'),
('115.17.b.22.D',4,'Fertilization happens when...','["a bone heals", "a seed grows", "a sperm cell joins an egg cell", "two eggs join"]'::jsonb,2,'Fertilization starts development.','original'),
('115.17.b.22.D',4,'Reproduction is the process of...','["breathing", "eating food", "sleeping", "making new living things"]'::jsonb,3,'Living things reproduce.','original'),
('115.17.b.22.E',4,'After fertilization, the developing baby is first called an embryo and later a...','["fetus", "seed", "sprout", "bud"]'::jsonb,0,'Developmental stage names.','original'),
('115.17.b.22.E',4,'During fetal development, the baby grows inside the mother in the...','["bone", "uterus", "stomach", "lung"]'::jsonb,1,'The uterus protects the baby.','original')
